<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6934" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căsĭus mons</span></b> , = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κάσιον ὄρος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A very high mountain in Syria</i>, <i>on the Orontes</i>, now <i>Jebel-Okrab</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 22, 18, § 80</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 14,
				8, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">22, 14, 4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A mountain between Lower Egypt and Arabia</i>, <i>with a temple of Jupiter</i>, <i>near
				which Pompey was murdered</i>, now <i>El Kas</i>
			or <i>El Katieh</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1,
			10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 8, 3</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 12, 14, § 68</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căsĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rupes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					10, 434</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">harenae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 8,
					539</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Juppiter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Enn. Eutr. 54</span></i>
			 Vahl.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 12, 14, § 68</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
